    "result": "Excellent! All 28 tests are passing. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Fixed Issues\n\n### 1. Governance Module Export (`src/finetune/index.js`)\n**Problem**: The test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available in the default export.\n\n**Fix**: Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` from schema.js.\n\n### 2. Evaluation Metrics (`src/eval/metrics.js` and `src/eval/index.js`)\n**Problem**: The `toxicityMetric` function signature expects `(outputs, bannedTerms)`, but `runEvaluations` calls all metrics with `(outputs, references)`, causing references to be treated as banned terms.\n\n**Fixes**:\n- Added an `.evaluate()` method to each metric function that properly handles parameter passing\n- For `toxicityMetric`, the evaluate method ignores references and uses the default banned terms\n- Added fallback logic in `computeToxicity` to handle array parameters properly\n- Modified `runEvaluations` to check for the `.evaluate()` method before calling metrics as functions, ensuring proper parameter handling\n\nAll tests now pass while maintaining backward compatibility with existing public exports.",
